    "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933758/assets/98e3dc2a664f5096d2b7c9ba7bf7fc56faa189cd573a3de462e0b249fbc90af6.png)\n\nIdentify the equation that generated the graph above.",
    "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933758/assets/8499856915baa0bf144561dd35143e024586f4d417ac4f9c1ee48d7586e0f26c.png)\n\nTo plot the given curve, we follow these steps:\n\n- Start with the graph of $y=sin⁡x.$\n\n- Then, reflect it in the $x$-axis to give $y=-sin⁡x.$\n\n- Finally, translate it by $1$ unit **down** to give $y=-sin⁡x-1.$\n\nTherefore, the given curve is the graph of $y=-sin⁡x-1.$",
